  <pre><code class="language-json">{`{
  "key": "ttml_lyrics:shape of you ed sheeran",
  "found": true,
  "type": "lyrics",
  "track_duration_ms": 233712,
  "score": 0.97,
  "language": "en",
  "isRTL": false,
  "ttml_length": 45678,
  "ttml_preview": "<?xml version=\\"1.0\\" encoding=\\"UTF-8\\"?>..."
}`}</code></pre>

  <h3>Response fields</h3>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Field</th>
        <th>Description</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><code>key</code></td>
        <td>The key that was inspected</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>found</code></td>
        <td>Whether an entry exists for the key</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>type</code></td>
        <td>
          <code>lyrics</code>, <code>no_lyrics_sentinel</code> (a stored "no lyrics" marker), or
          <code>negative_cache</code>. Only when <code>found</code> is <code>true</code>.
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>reason</code></td>
        <td>Why no lyrics were found. Only when <code>type</code> is <code>negative_cache</code>.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>track_duration_ms</code>, <code>score</code>, <code>language</code>, <code>isRTL</code></td>
        <td>Stored metadata. Only when <code>type</code> is <code>lyrics</code>.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>ttml_length</code>, <code>ttml_preview</code></td>
        <td>Length of the stored lyrics and their first 300 characters. Only when <code>type</code> is <code>lyrics</code>.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>Without the <code>key</code> parameter, the response is <code>400</code> with <code>{`{"error": "Provide 'key' parameter"}`}</code>.</p>

  <h2>GET /cache/clear</h2>
  <p>Delete all cached lyrics and negative cache entries, for every provider. This cannot be undone through the API.</p>

  <h3>Example</h3>
  <CodeTabs tabs={[
    { language: 'curl', code: `curl -H "Authorization: token" \\
  "https://api.betterlyrics.org/cache/clear"` },
    { language: 'javascript', code: `const res = await fetch("https://api.betterlyrics.org/cache/clear", {
  headers: { "Authorization": "token" },
});
const data = await res.json();` },
    { language: 'python', code: `import requests

res = requests.get(
    "https://api.betterlyrics.org/cache/clear",
    headers={"Authorization": "token"},
)
data = res.json()` },
    { language: 'go', code: `package main

import (
	"fmt"
	"io"
	"net/http"
)

func main() {
	req, err := http.NewRequest(http.MethodGet, "https://api.betterlyrics.org/cache/clear", nil)
	if err != nil {
		panic(err)
	}
	req.Header.Set("Authorization", "token")

	res, err := http.DefaultClient.Do(req)
	if err != nil {
		panic(err)
	}
	defer res.Body.Close()

	body, err := io.ReadAll(res.Body)
	if err != nil {
		panic(err)
	}
	fmt.Println(string(body))
}` },
  ]} />

  <pre><code class="language-json">{`{
  "message": "Cache cleared successfully"
}`}</code></pre>

  <h2>GET /cache/clear/{`{provider}`}</h2>
  <p>
    Delete cached lyrics and negative cache entries for one provider. <code>provider</code> is one of
    <code>ttml</code>, <code>kugou</code>, <code>qq</code> or <code>legacy</code>.
  </p>

  <h3>Example</h3>
  <CodeTabs tabs={[
    { language: 'curl', code: `curl -H "Authorization: token" \\
  "https://api.betterlyrics.org/cache/clear/kugou"` },
    { language: 'javascript', code: `const res = await fetch("https://api.betterlyrics.org/cache/clear/kugou", {
  headers: { "Authorization": "token" },
});
const data = await res.json();` },
    { language: 'python', code: `import requests

res = requests.get(
    "https://api.betterlyrics.org/cache/clear/kugou",
    headers={"Authorization": "token"},
)
data = res.json()` },
    { language: 'go', code: `package main

import (
	"fmt"
	"io"
	"net/http"
)

func main() {
	req, err := http.NewRequest(http.MethodGet, "https://api.betterlyrics.org/cache/clear/kugou", nil)
	if err != nil {
		panic(err)
	}
	req.Header.Set("Authorization", "token")

	res, err := http.DefaultClient.Do(req)
	if err != nil {
		panic(err)
	}
	defer res.Body.Close()

	body, err := io.ReadAll(res.Body)
	if err != nil {
		panic(err)
	}
	fmt.Println(string(body))
}` },
  ]} />

  <pre><code class="language-json">{`{
  "message": "Cleared cache for provider: kugou",
  "provider": "kugou",
  "keys_deleted": 1234
}`}</code></pre>
  <p><code>keys_deleted</code> counts the deleted lyrics entries. An unknown provider returns <code>400</code>:</p>
  <pre><code class="language-json">{`{
  "error": "Unknown provider: foo",
  "valid_providers": ["ttml", "kugou", "qq", "legacy"]
}`}</code></pre>
  <p>A database error on either clear endpoint returns <code>500</code> with an <code>error</code> field.</p>

  <h2 id="removed-endpoints">Removed endpoints</h2>
  <p>
    <code>/cache/backup</code>, <code>/cache/backups</code>, <code>/cache/restore</code>, <code>/cache/dump</code>,
    <code>/cache/migrate</code> and <code>/cache/migrate/status</code> are removed. Backups are handled by the
    database platform. With a valid token they return <code>410 Gone</code>:
  </p>
  <pre><code class="language-json">{`{
  "error": "Endpoint removed",
  "message": "This operation is not available on the managed Postgres backend. Backups and point-in-time recovery are handled by the platform."
}`}</code></pre>
  <p>
    <code>/cache</code> is also removed. It needs no token and returns <code>410 Gone</code> with <code>error</code>,
    <code>message</code> and an <code>alternatives</code> object.
  </p>

  <h2>Notes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>These endpoints are for administrative use only</li>
    <li>Lyrics cache entries do not expire. They stay until they are cleared.</li>
    <li>The cache access token is different from the API key</li>
  </ul>
</DocsLayout>
